# What claude-test.sh runs: one Claude session per layout (reachable, top), each with its cases, and each session's bounds.
# A case runs in both layouts only when the layouts render it differently; the rest run in one.
# entries-<layout> (optional) tells that session which directory entries and names its cases use, so none meets an entry already known.
# backend: yes when the cases use the test backend; a run that asks for Claude must then start it too.
backend: yes
model: claude-haiku-5-5
layouts: reachable top
cases-reachable: U1, U2, U4, D15 and W12
cases-top: U2, U4 and D15 (the list's order and the row's flip differ in this layout)
entries-reachable: the smoke test joined the channel ci_cards; U1 and U4 search `ci_cards`, U2 and W12 search `ci cards` (the space keeps the local list from matching it); D15 searches `ci seed` and long-presses #ci_group, closing the menu without choosing Open; open and join nothing else
entries-top: the same entries: U4 searches `ci_cards`, U2 searches `ci cards`, D15 long-presses #ci_group from `ci seed`; nothing else is opened or joined
max-turns: 300
max-budget-usd: 3
